Orchbee owns local rule corrections, its parser and sampling integration.
grok.toml adds browser-authentication blockers and an uncertain-login guard, with updated version metadata.
gemini.toml adds a folder-trust blocker and a composer idle rule, with updated version metadata.
kilo.toml adds a prompt-footer idle rule, with updated version metadata.
hermes.toml adds a busy-footer working rule and a composer idle rule, with updated version metadata.
kimi.toml accepts an ellipsis character after the spinner status word, with updated version metadata.
cline.toml reads the spinner status anywhere on the live screen and drops the catch-all working rule, with updated
version metadata.
opencode.toml and pi.toml add live-footer idle and status-loader working rules, with updated version metadata.
mimo.toml adapts opencode.toml's OpenCode 1.x rules to MiMo Code, which is built on OpenCode 1.x: its spinner and brand
replace OpenCode's in the working rules, and it adds a workspace-trust blocker, an interrupt-footer working rule and a
prompt-footer idle rule.
atomcode.toml, codebuddy.toml, command-code.toml, deveco.toml, jcode.toml, minimax-code.toml, mothx.toml, omp.toml,
openclaw.toml, prime-agent.toml, reasonix.toml and snow.toml are authored by Orchbee and are not derived from Herdr.
The region matching implementation is adapted from src/detect/manifest.rs, with UTF-8-safe CRLF offsets.
